# Shared content and assets

- Edit canonical prayer content, datasets, images, fonts, and schemas under `Shared/` first.
- Regenerate or sync platform copies with the repository tools; never hand-edit generated packs or
  platform dataset copies.
- Keep built-in `.prosaryprayer` packs byte-identical to `Shared/dist` and self-contained for
  import/export.
- Store prayer artwork only inside the packs. Do not duplicate it in asset catalogs, Android
  resources, or Windows assets; retain only documented native fallback artwork.
- Keep `LICENSE` at the repository root as the single license for all original Prosary material,
  including native and web apps, shared data, documentation, tools, and assets. Link to it rather
  than creating platform-specific copies; third-party material retains its original license.
- Update all three native loaders, schemas, and tests together when a shared contract changes.
- Run the shared validators and asset-deduplication audit before committing.
